      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module classifies repository files and, for tabular data files available locally, extracts each column's type and summary statistics.",
          "#### Data Tree",
          "Where the files sit within each repository. Each file is followed by how it was classified, which study it belongs to.",
          "**Repository: https://osf.io/archi**",
          "```\n├── extra.csv.gz/\n│   └── extra.csv    📊 data\n├── results.tar.gz/\n│   └── summary.csv  📊 data\n├── bundle.zip       ❓ unknown\n├── README.md        📄 readme\n└── stimuli.zip      📁 materials ex1\n```",
          "#### Data Files",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## summary.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(block = 1:4, acc = c(0.9, 0.85, 0.95, 0.8)), row.names = c(NA, \n4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## extra.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(item = c(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"), value = 1:3), row.names = c(NA, \n3L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Descriptives Overview\n\nWe found 0 columns with at least one missing value.",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## summary.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"acc\", \"block\"), Representation = c(\"numeric\", \n\"numeric\"), Level = c(\"ratio\", \"ratio\"), Concept = c(\"\", \"\"), \n    Role = c(\"measure\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\"), Rows = c(4L, \n    4L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(4L, 4L), Mean = c(0.875, \n    2.5), SD = c(0.065, 1.291), Min = c(0.8, 1), Max = c(0.95, \n    4)), row.names = c(\"acc\", \"block\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n## extra.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"item\", \"value\"), Representation = c(\"text\", \n\"numeric\"), Level = c(\"nominal\", \"ratio\"), Concept = c(\"\", \"\"\n), Role = c(\"measure\", \"measure\"), Unit = c(\"\", \"\"), Rows = c(3L, \n3L), \"% Missing\" = c(0, 0), \"N Unique\" = c(3L, 3L), Mean = c(NA, \n2), SD = c(NA, 1), Min = c(NA, 1), Max = c(NA, 3)), row.names = c(\"item\", \n\"value\"), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "This module runs automated data-quality checks (outliers, miscoded missing values, empty and constant columns, SPSS filter variables, category casing, problematic column names, mixed text encodings, spreadsheet formatting) on the extracted data files.",
          "We examined 4 columns across 2 data files.",
          "#### Careless Responding",
          "No file could be screened for careless responding.",
          "**What this does not cover.** Only 0 of 2 data files could be screened: the rest had no detectable multi-item scale block, or too few respondents. Even in a screened file, these checks only look at multi-item rating scales — the only place where a repeated or flat answer pattern is interpretable. Single questions, open text, demographics and any item outside a detected scale block are never examined. A respondent can therefore answer most of a survey carelessly and still not be flagged here, and finding nothing is not evidence that a dataset is free of careless responding."
        ]
